# Lesson 5, new exercise: opener shows hearts, partner has spades.
title: Hearts, but partner has spades
id: L05-11
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.2, 5.6
student: S
board: 22
dealer: E
vulnerable: EW

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  A762   Q54    J65    A73
  E  K93    J7     A872   Q962
  S  Q85    AK98   KQ3    K84
  W  JT4    T632   T94    JT5

auction:
  E Pass
  S 1NT*   = 15-17 points, balanced
     not *: 17 points and a balanced hand: open 1NT.
  W Pass
  N 2C     = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
  E Pass
  S 2H*    = Four hearts
     key: Four hearts, so bid 2♥.
     not 2D: 2♦ says "no 4-card major." You have four hearts.
  W Pass
  N 3NT    = Game values, four spades, not four hearts
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = No spade fit: 3NT is right
     key: North has spades, not hearts. You have only three spades, so pass.
     not 4S: You have only three spades.
     not 4H: North's 3NT says "not hearts."
  W Pass

auction recap:
  You showed hearts. North's 3NT said "game values, but not hearts," so
  North's major is spades. You have only three spades, so there is no fit, and
  you pass. South is declarer, because South bid no-trump first, and so West
  will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  winners: 6
  remind: What is the contract?

play:
  1   W SJ  N S2  E S3  S SQ*
      SQ key: Win the trick with the queen.
      SQ not S8: Did you notice your queen wins this trick? Ducking gives the defense a chance to set up spades.
      SQ not S5: Did you notice your queen wins this trick? Ducking gives the defense a chance to set up spades.
  2   S DK*  W D4  N D5  E DA
      DK key: Knock out the ace to set up your diamonds.
      DK not CK: Did you look for where your extra tricks come from? Diamonds need the ace knocked out first.
      note: Knock out the ♦A to set up diamond tricks.
  3   E CQ  S C4  W C5  N CA
  4   N SA  E S9  S S5  W S4
      note: Take the ace of spades.
  5   N H5  E H7  S HA  W H2
      note: Now the hearts: lead toward your ace-king.
  6   S HK  W H3  N H4  E HJ
      note: Take the other top heart.
  7   S H9  W H6  N HQ  E D2
      note: Over to dummy's queen of hearts.
  8   N S7  E SK  S S8  W ST
      note: Lead a spade to set up dummy's long spade.
  9   E C9  S CK  W CT  N C3
  10  S DQ  W D9  N D6  E D7
      note: Now cash your diamond winners.
  11  S D3  W DT  N DJ  E D8
      note: Over to dummy's jack of diamonds.
  12  N S6  E C2  S C8  W HT
      note: Dummy's last spade is a winner.
  13  N C7  E C6  S H8  W CJ
      note: 10 tricks: 3NT made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  The plan: knock out the ♦A to set up extra diamond tricks, then cash the
  rest. Winning the first spade with the queen keeps the defense from
  setting up their spades first.

  3NT made with an overtrick. With no 4-4 major fit, no-trump was the right place to
  play. Stayman did its job: it checked for a fit, found none, and still
  reached the right game.
